<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2858" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antĭdŏtum</span></b> , i,
			n., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ŏs</span></b> , i,
			f. (cf. <i><span class="en">Scrib. Larg. Comp. 99, 106</span></i>, and passages
		cited there), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίδοτον</span> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ος</span>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a counterpoison.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antidota raro, sed interdum necessaria sunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					5, 23</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 1, 14, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">se antidotum daturum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 7, 2, 25</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ner. 34 al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antidotus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					17, 16</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Dig. 18, 1, 35</span></i>.—Sometimes, in
			gen., <i>an antidote</i>, <i>remedy</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Spart. Hadr.
			23</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antidotum adversus Caesarem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 29</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
